statement:
Let $u:Y\to X$, $v:Z\to Y$, $w:T\to Z$ be morphisms of schemes [def-pc-scheme], with small etale sites [def-weil-pbc-etale-site], categories of abelian sheaves $\Ab(-_{\Et})$ [def-weil-pbc-abelian-etale-sheaves] and direct images $s_*$, $(s_*F)(W)=F(W\times_ST)$ for $s:T\to S$ and $W$ an object of $S_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-direct-image]. For composable $s:S'\to S$, $t:S''\to S'$ let $d_{s,t}:(s\circ t)_*\xrightarrow{\sim}s_*\circ t_*$ be the isomorphism of functors whose component at a sheaf $F$ on $S''_{\Et}$ and an object $W$ of $S_{\Et}$ is $F$ applied to the canonical isomorphism $(W\times_SS')\times_{S'}S''\xrightarrow{\sim}W\times_SS''$ of objects of $S''_{\Et}$ [def-pc-fibre-product], and let $d_S:(\mathrm{id}_S)_*\xrightarrow{\sim}\mathrm{id}$ be given by the canonical isomorphisms $W\xrightarrow{\sim}W\times_SS$ (these are the isomorphisms $d$ of [lem-weil-pbc-inverse-image-composition] (1), (3)). Then

1. (Associativity.) $(u_*d_{v,w})\circ d_{u,v\circ w}=(d_{u,v}w_*)\circ d_{u\circ v,w}:\ (u\circ v\circ w)_*\to u_*v_*w_*$;
2. (Unit laws.) $(d_Xu_*)\circ d_{\mathrm{id}_X,u}=\mathrm{id}_{u_*}$ and $(u_*d_Y)\circ d_{u,\mathrm{id}_Y}=\mathrm{id}_{u_*}$ as transformations $u_*\to u_*$.
